report.custom / 01M3P4SZY21WZ19A704G7CK5NV / attempt 1
Informe de sitios a bloquear (Polla Chilena)

INPUT
  attachments verified against request.json sha256: spec.md, dataset.json.gz, dataset.csv -> 3/3 match
  dataset.csv (chile_28_08_26.csv) parsed as semicolon-delimited UTF-8; all 9 expected columns present
  30,151 records read; 13 duplicate URLs dropped; 0 blank records
  status: Illegal gambling 14,433 / Review needed 10,499 / Not gambling 4,720 / Unreachable 499

POPULATION (regla 1 and regla 5)
  the export's legality label in Status is renamed Juego and stated once in the report's
  terminology note, so the counts still reconcile with the original file.
  evaluated population = Illegal gambling + Review needed = 24,919 records. Rule 5 requires the
  unvalidated rows to be included, so pending-review variants are in; 1,779 of the proposals are
  pending. Not gambling and Unreachable are excluded and both counts are stated under Límites.

BRAND ATTRIBUTION (regla 2)
  the two embedded tables parse to 23 denounced brands over 90 distinct domains and 101 denunciation
  records, and 31 monitored brands. Both figures match the spec's own stated totals.
  Source lineage Variant(x)/Redirect(x) is resolved to the root with cycle control; mean chain depth
  5.3, maximum 21. Long chains are real: 09bet.app > 11bet.app > 1qbet.app > ... > 6xbet.org >
  1xbet.com is a single-character rotation network, which is why 1xBet carries 1,907 proposals.
  the brand goes to the root of the chain as rule 2 requires. The motivo, by contrast, describes the
  relation actually observed, against the brand token when the name carries it and otherwise against
  the immediate parent. An earlier version derived the motivo from the root token and labelled 69%
  of all proposals a typosquat, which was an artefact of that choice, not a finding.
  near-spelling fallback is deliberately strict (length >= 6, same first three characters, one edit
  or Jaro-Winkler >= 0.96). A looser version attributed apuestasvzla.com to Apuestas Royal and
  bet.cc to Bet365 on a shared generic prefix.

CHILE RELEVANCE (regla 4)
  Alta 89, Media 1,423, Baja 1,678.
  Spanish and Portuguese are separated on vocabulary that differs between them; "depósito" is never
  used as a Spanish signal, as the spec requires. 224 proposals carry Portuguese and are placed in
  Baja on that basis.
  Baja requires positive evidence of another market. 2,829 proposals carry no determinable content
  language, almost always because the page was down, blocked or parked, so a generic suffix
  reachable from Chile stays Media and the report says how many cases that is, so Media reads as
  reachability rather than as a content finding.
  'chile', 'chil' and 'latam' are matched as substrings; 'cl' and 'lat' only when delimited. As bare
  substrings they promoted kenyaconsulatela.com to Alta on the 'lat' inside "consulate".

MANUAL VERIFICATION (as the spec's checklist requires)
  10 records reviewed against their LLM Reasoning. Three defects found and fixed: Media was being
  assigned without the Spanish-content test; transposition typosquats (ggpoker -> ggpkoer) were
  labelled "marca embebida" because the edit test did not cover transpositions; and a domain whose
  stem equals the brand token defaulted to "rotación de TLD" even when the suffix was the brand's
  own. A second sample of 10 was reviewed after the fixes with no further defects.

CHECKLIST BEFORE DELIVERY — all pass
  no occurrence of ilegal / ilícito / con licencia / sin licencia outside the terminology note
  CSV rows (3,190) equal the summary total and equal the rows rendered in the report tables
  no CSV domain appears in the denounced table, compared by registrable domain (111 excluded)
  every row carries a motivo from the permitted list and an estado_marca
  nothing attributed to skillonnet.com, 418services.com, baytreeinteractive.com or kaizengaming.com
  every URL comes from the export; none invented
  aguasanjoaquin.cl excluded as a seed: it is a Chilean water utility, not operator property

OUTPUT
  report.html: self-contained, A4 via @page, no horizontal overflow at 1000 px or at 390 px,
  light and dark schemes, one h1, jump-link contents. Checked in Chromium at both widths and
  printed to PDF at 210 x 297 mm.
  sitios-propuestos.csv: UTF-8 with BOM, 3,190 rows, ordered by relevancia then marca then dominio,
  columns exactly as SALIDA 2 specifies.
  0 legitimate compromised sites were found; that section states so explicitly rather than being
  dropped.

STORAGE
  git-lfs is not available in this environment, so assets are committed to git directly and
  storage.kind is "git", matching every earlier result in this repository.
